{"case":"toctou_after_reap","client_pid":258591,"liveness_after_reap":"gone","note":"the socket is still open; SO_PEERCRED still reports this pid","pid_dir_exists_after_reap":false,"reaped_by_server":true}
{"case":"toctou_impostor","detail":{"attempted":false}}

# T1b — the server forces a BRAND NEW process onto the dead client's pid
# via ns_last_pid, which needs a private pid namespace. This is the
# adversarial case: pid reused while the socket is still open.
\$ unshare -Urpf --mount-proc credprobe toctou --impostor

